Describe the Bug
An input field declared strawberry.Maybe[str | None] (what schema-codegen itself now emits for nullable input fields, after #4178) comes out of strawberry codegen doubly wrapped: Optional[Optional[str]]. It is valid Python, but it is noisy and reads as a codegen bug in generated client code.
Reproduction
Run in an empty directory with strawberry-graphql[cli] installed:
cat > app.py <<'PY'
import strawberry


@strawberry.input
class UpdateInput:
    title: strawberry.Maybe[str | None]


@strawberry.type
class Query:
    hello: str = "world"


@strawberry.type
class Mutation:
    @strawberry.mutation
    def update(self, input: UpdateInput) -> str:
        return "ok"


schema = strawberry.Schema(query=Query, mutation=Mutation)
PY
cat > update.graphql <<'GQL'
mutation Update($input: UpdateInput!) {
  update(input: $input)
}
GQL
mkdir -p out
strawberry codegen --schema app:schema -o out -p python update.graphql > /dev/null
cat out/update.py
Actual
class UpdateInput:
    title: Optional[Optional[str]] = None
Expected
class UpdateInput:
    title: Optional[str] = None
System Information

Operating system: Linux x86_64 (Amazon Linux 2023)
Python version: 3.11.16
Strawberry version (if applicable): 0.336.2 (latest), graphql-core 3.3.0. Also reproduces on 0.328.2.

Additional Context
Related: #4178. Since schema-codegen emits Maybe[X | None] for every nullable input field, this affects every input when the two commands are chained.

Describe the Bug
schema-codegen emits every field as a plain attribute and drops its arguments, both on root types and on nested object types. That has two consequences:

The generated schema no longer matches the SDL (issue(id: ID!) becomes issue: Issue | None, comments(first: Int) becomes comments: list[str]).
Input types referenced only through arguments are no longer reachable from the schema. strawberry codegen against the generated schema then fails for any operation whose variables use them, which covers every mutation with an input: argument.

Reproduction
Run in an empty directory with strawberry-graphql[cli] installed:
cat > schema.graphql <<'GQL'
input IssueCreateInput {
  title: String!
}

type Issue {
  id: ID!
  comments(first: Int): [String!]!
}

type Query {
  issue(id: ID!): Issue
}

type Mutation {
  issueCreate(input: IssueCreateInput!): Issue
}
GQL
strawberry schema-codegen schema.graphql -o generated.py
grep -n -A3 "class Issue:\|class Query:\|class Mutation:" generated.py

cat > create.graphql <<'GQL'
mutation Create($input: IssueCreateInput!) {
  issueCreate(input: $input) { id }
}
GQL
mkdir -p out
