Description
Strawberry has extend=True support on @strawberry.type, and the underlying object definition can store extend=True even when is_input=True is used internally. However, input object type extensions are not fully supported today:

@strawberry.input(...) does not expose an extend parameter.
@strawberry.type(is_input=True, extend=True) stores the flag, but printed SDL still emits input Foo, not extend input Foo.
Defining a base input and an extension input with the same GraphQL name fails as a duplicate type name.

This matters for schema composition/stitching and addon-style systems where one package defines a base input and another package needs to contribute fields to it. In particular, this came up while evaluating whether strawberry-graphql-django could expose extend=True for strawberry_django.input(...) in the same way it already exposes it for output types. The Django integration can pass the option through, but the correct owner for the SDL/converter behavior seems to be Strawberry core.
